---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us | SaveEditor.Online"
  description="Learn about the team behind SaveEditor.Online - a free, browser-based game save editing tool for compatible local saves."
>
  <section class="container mx-auto px-4 py-12 max-w-6xl">
    <div class="text-center mb-16">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-6 text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
        About SaveEditor.Online
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        An open-source initiative empowering gamers with the freedom to play their way. A
        browser-based save file editor focused on compatible local saves, clear limits, and backups.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 mb-16">
      <div
        class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700 text-center"
      >
        <div class="text-4xl font-bold text-primary-600 mb-2">Browser</div>
        <div class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 font-medium">Main Editing Flow</div>
      </div>
      <div
        class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700 text-center"
      >
        <div class="text-4xl font-bold text-primary-600 mb-2">50+</div>
        <div class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 font-medium">Supported Formats</div>
      </div>
      <div
        class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700 text-center"
      >
        <div class="text-4xl font-bold text-primary-600 mb-2">Free</div>
        <div class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 font-medium">Forever Open</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
      <section class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Our Mission</h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
          SaveEditor.Online was created with a simple but powerful goal: <strong
            >to democratize game modification</strong
          >. We believe that single-player gaming is a personal experience. Whether you want to skip
          a tedious grind, recover a corrupted save file, or experiment with different story paths,
          you should have practical tools and clear limits before changing a save.
        </p>
        <p class="leading-relaxed mt-4">
          In the past, editing save files required downloading sketchy software, hex editing, or
          complex technical knowledge. We changed that by building an editor that runs directly in
          your web browser. No downloads or installations; keep a backup before editing.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-16 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-12">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Why Trust Us?</h2>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">🔒 Client-Side Technology</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              File handling is designed around browser-side parsing. When you select a file, it is
              loaded into your browser's memory, edited, and saved back to your disk in the main
              editing flow. We do use Google Analytics and AdSense
              for site performance and ads; see our Privacy and Cookie policies for details.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">🛡️ Transparent & Safe</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              We are committed to transparency. Our tool is built on modern web standards (HTML5,
              WebAssembly) and is regularly updated to improve compatibility. We strictly
              oppose cheating in multiplayer games and design our tools solely for single-player
              experiences.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Supported Technologies</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          We are constantly expanding our support for game engines and file formats. Our current
          capabilities include:
        </p>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
          <div
            class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-lg"
          >
            <span class="text-2xl">🎮</span>
            <div>
              <div class="font-bold">RPG Maker</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">.rpgsave (MV/MZ)</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div
            class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-lg"
          >
            <span class="text-2xl">🎲</span>
            <div>
              <div class="font-bold">Unity</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">PlayerPrefs, JSON</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div
            class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-lg"
          >
            <span class="text-2xl">⚡</span>
            <div>
              <div class="font-bold">Unreal Engine</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">.sav (GVAS)</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div
            class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-lg"
          >
            <span class="text-2xl">🎭</span>
            <div>
              <div class="font-bold">Ren'Py</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">.save (Viewer)</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div
            class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-lg"
          >
            <span class="text-2xl">👾</span>
            <div>
              <div class="font-bold">GameMaker</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">.ini, .json</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div
            class="flex items-center gap-3 p-4 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-lg"
          >
            <span class="text-2xl">📝</span>
            <div>
              <div class="font-bold">NaniNovel</div>
              <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">.nson</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <details
            class="group bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-xl p-6 cursor-pointer"
          >
            <summary class="font-bold text-lg flex justify-between items-center list-none">
              <span>Is SaveEditor.Online really free?</span>
              <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180">
                <svg
                  fill="none"
                  height="24"
                  shape-rendering="geometricPrecision"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  stroke-width="1.5"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  width="24"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg
                >
              </span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
              Yes, the editor is free to use. We are ad-supported which allows us to keep the
              service available.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details
            class="group bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-xl p-6 cursor-pointer"
          >
            <summary class="font-bold text-lg flex justify-between items-center list-none">
              <span>Is my data safe?</span>
              <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180">
                <svg
                  fill="none"
                  height="24"
                  shape-rendering="geometricPrecision"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  stroke-width="1.5"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  width="24"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg
                >
              </span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
              Browser-side parsing is the default model for the main editor. We do use Google
              Analytics and AdSense for site performance and ads;
              see our Privacy and Cookie policies.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details
            class="group bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-xl p-6 cursor-pointer"
          >
            <summary class="font-bold text-lg flex justify-between items-center list-none">
              <span>Will using this tool get me banned?</span>
              <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180">
                <svg
                  fill="none"
                  height="24"
                  shape-rendering="geometricPrecision"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  stroke-width="1.5"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  width="24"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg
                >
              </span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
              For single-player games, no. We do not support or encourage cheating in online or
              multiplayer games.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details
            class="group bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 rounded-xl p-6 cursor-pointer"
          >
            <summary class="font-bold text-lg flex justify-between items-center list-none">
              <span>Can you add support for a specific game?</span>
              <span class="transition group-open:rotate-180">
                <svg
                  fill="none"
                  height="24"
                  shape-rendering="geometricPrecision"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  stroke-width="1.5"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  width="24"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg
                >
              </span>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
              Let us know via our contact form! We prioritize based on user demand and technical
              feasibility.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script type="application/ld+json">
  [
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "SaveEditor.Online",
      "url": "https://saveeditor.top",
      "logo": "https://saveeditor.top/favicon.svg",
      "sameAs": ["https://github.com/paradoxie/saveeditor"],
      "contactPoint": {
        "@type": "ContactPoint",
        "email": "support@saveeditor.top",
        "contactType": "customer support"
      },
      "foundingDate": "2024",
      "slogan": "Empowering gamers with the freedom to play their way."
    },
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is SaveEditor.Online really free?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, the editor is free to use. We are ad-supported which allows us to keep the service available."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is my data safe?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Browser-side parsing is the default model for the main editor. We use Google Analytics and AdSense for site performance and ads; see our Privacy and Cookie policies."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Will using this tool get me banned?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For single-player games, no. We do not support or encourage cheating in online or multiplayer games."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can you add support for a specific game?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Let us know via our contact form! We prioritize based on user demand and technical feasibility."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
</script>
